From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:09:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(accounting): name executor completion and bounded call
 CPU [daveey]

Why: mature Mac snapshots still show about 2.2% of one core in the
concurrent.futures worker outside submitted-function scopes. Work item
completion runs synchronous Future callbacks after the function scope ends.
The deadline worker also hides its callable behind an unscoped closure.

Wrap the original CPython work item run (legacy and task-triple layouts)
in an exclusive executor_item/<logical function> scope. Existing nested
thread scopes retain their own CPU; the item scope records the remainder.
Name bounded-sync calls without altering deadlines or context. Diagnostic
entry, naming and booking failures must not skip/retry operations, replace
their exceptions or kill pool workers. Raise bounded target capacity to256.

Proof:
- Initial completion/cap RED:2 failures,2 controls passed. Expanded RED
  also fails the previously unnamed bounded call.
- Final23 importing suites:439 passed,13 skipped,0 failed.
- Eleven exact-anchor mutants killed, baseline44 passed: swapped native
  user/system fields, list/iterator attribution gaps, cap, missing scopes,
  disabled toggles, and diagnostic enter/exit/name failures.
- Native Linux syscall/user split test plus synthetic unequal proc fields.
- Full staged scripts/check --base origin/main passes.
- Independent precommit review's diagnostic-failure findings addressed;
  exact-head review and CI still required before landing.

No optimization or causal live CPU reduction claimed. Queue/semaphore costs
remain outside the item scope; natural Mac deployment and mature idle
readback are still owed by t_84a411c80a478c57.
